---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import SocialLinks from "../components/SocialLinks.astro";
import { site } from "../config/site";
---

<BaseLayout
  title={`About — ${site.name}`}
  description="About my approach to software engineering, mobile products, distributed systems, and machine learning."
>
  <div class="shell page-shell">
    <div class="page-intro">
      <p class="eyebrow">About / The person behind the work</p>
      <h1>Curious about the whole system.</h1>
      <p>
        I’m a software engineer interested in what happens when good ideas meet
        real constraints: users, reliability, performance, and the work of
        keeping things running.
      </p>
    </div>
    <div class="about-grid">
      <div class="prose">
        <h2>How I work</h2>
        <p>
          I like projects where product thinking and technical depth reinforce
          each other. That might mean shaping an intuitive mobile experience,
          untangling an API boundary, or making an ML workflow repeatable enough
          to trust.
        </p>
        <p>
          I value clear communication, small feedback loops, and solutions that
          a team can understand after the first version ships.
        </p>
        <h2>Current focus</h2>
        <p>
          These days I’m especially interested in production machine learning:
          data quality, evaluation, model serving, and the infrastructure around
          useful predictions.
        </p>
        <p>
          I bring more than 15 years of production software experience from
          games and mobile products to this work, with the same attention to
          performance, reliability, and user feedback.
        </p>
        <h2 id="work-experience">Work Experience</h2>
        <p>
          MacroPinch and NoSixFive share owners and a workplace. My roles
          overlap because the work grew from iOS and backend development into
          Unity games after MacroPinch supported me in learning Unity.
        </p>
        <ol class="work-list">
          <li>
            <span class="work-date">Oct 2017 – Present</span>
            <div>
              <h3>Game Developer</h3>
              <p class="work-company">
                NoSixFive · Full-time · Sofia, Bulgaria
              </p>
              <p class="work-detail">
                I developed Train Merger as a solo Unity developer; it has
                reached more than 1 million downloads. My game work also
                includes Cosmo Run (1M+ downloads), Jump Drive, Don Zombie, and,
                more recently, Candy Champions.
              </p>
              <p class="work-projects">
                Projects:
                <a href="/projects/candy-champions/">Candy Champions</a> ·
                <a href="/projects/cosmo-run/">Cosmo Run</a> ·
                <a href="/projects/train-merger/">Train Merger</a> ·
                <a href="/projects/jump-drive/">Jump Drive</a>
              </p>
            </div>
          </li>
          <li>
            <span class="work-date">Sep 2013 – Present</span>
            <div>
              <h3>iOS &amp; Backend Developer</h3>
              <p class="work-company">MacroPinch · Sofia, Bulgaria</p>
              <p class="work-detail">
                Alongside iOS development, I built the backends for MyGrocery
                and Outwalk. For Outwalk, I coordinated two Android developers,
                two iOS developers, a QA specialist, and two UI/UX designers.
              </p>
              <p class="work-projects">
                Projects:
                <a href="/projects/vng-tg/">VideoNystagmoGraph To Go</a> ·
                <a href="/projects/outwalk/">Outwalk</a> ·
                <a href="/projects/cardiograph/">Cardiograph</a>
              </p>
            </div>
          </li>
          <li>
            <span class="work-date">Feb 2012 – Sep 2013</span>
            <div>
              <h3>PHP Developer</h3>
              <p class="work-company">Creative Web Bulgaria</p>
              <p class="work-detail">
                I built websites, online stores, Facebook applications, and
                social features with PHP, MySQL, HTML, CSS, and JavaScript. I
                extended CWeb CMS and its e-commerce modules, integrated
                YouTube, Vimeo, and Google Maps APIs, and contributed to an iOS
                app.
              </p>
            </div>
          </li>
        </ol>
        <h2>Education</h2>
        <p>
          I have a master’s degree in Software Technologies from Sofia
          University. My thesis focused on developing a conference management
          system, which later evolved into a deployed project for the Balkan
          Journal of Philosophy.
        </p>
        <p>
          I don’t see the degree itself as a direct measure of professional
          success, but it gave me several things I value. It taught me to write
          more clearly, encouraged me to explore ideas beyond my immediate
          field, and broadened my interests and perspective. It also gave me the
          opportunity to work with younger talent, which I found surprisingly
          refreshing.
        </p>
        <ol class="education-list">
          <li>
            <span class="education-date">Oct 2021 – Mar 2023</span>
            <div>
              <h3>Sofia University “St. Kliment Ohridski”</h3>
              <p class="education-degree">
                Master’s degree · Software Technologies
              </p>
            </div>
          </li>
          <li>
            <span class="education-date">2011 – 2015</span>
            <div>
              <h3>New Bulgarian University</h3>
              <p class="education-degree">
                Bachelor’s degree · Computer Science
              </p>
            </div>
          </li>
          <li>
            <span class="education-date">2006 – 2011</span>
            <div>
              <h3>Second English Language School “Thomas Jefferson”</h3>
              <p class="education-degree">Debate Team · Web Design</p>
              <p class="education-detail">
                Received an award for active participation in extracurricular
                activities.
              </p>
            </div>
          </li>
        </ol>
        <h2>A Nice Surprise</h2>
        <p>
          I just Googled myself and found something really cool: my high school
          is still hosting my personal website from 2010.
        </p>
        <p>
          It’s a small piece of my early development history that I had
          completely forgotten about. Pretty awesome to find it still online
          after all these years.
        </p>
        <p>
          <a href="https://2els.com/investicia-v-badeshteto/clubwd/portfolios/vmirchev/index.html">
            View the website ↗
          </a>
        </p>
      </div>
      <aside class="about-aside">
        <p class="eyebrow">Areas of practice</p>
        <ul>
          <li>Software Engineering</li>
          <li>Mobile Development</li>
          <li>Game Development</li>
          <li>Backend / Distributed Systems</li>
          <li>Machine Learning</li>
          <li>ML Engineering Projects</li>
        </ul>
        <p class="eyebrow">Elsewhere</p>
        <SocialLinks />
        <a class="aside-email" href={`mailto:${site.email}`}>
          {site.email} ↗
        </a>
      </aside>
    </div>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>
